                        "entry_id": "c8fb8909-7943-3aaa-80ed-65fd0c3801ca",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of a class of organic compounds of sulphur, ( R₁.S.R₂ ); they tend to be foul-smelling. When R₂ is a hydrogen atom, they are termed thiols or thioalcohols."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "57ce6574-9fcf-4d89-9822-aa753f6c3371",
                                "sense_id": "5cf4e580-b3ae-3ade-aced-9ecc8746220f",
                                "text": "Though this might come as a surprise, gas actually has no odor; gas companies are obligated to odorize it to make it safer for use in homes.\nMercaptan, a harmless chemical, is added to create the distinct smell in both natural gas (methane) and liquid petroleum gas (propane, butane)."
                            }
                        ]
